 ## Background
-The concept of dynamic neural radiance fields emerged shortly after the introduction of static NeRF. Early works like Space-Time Neural Irradiance Fields (ST-NIF) [S4, unofficial] and NeRFlow [S4, unofficial] demonstrated that time could be incorporated as an additional input dimension. Subsequent methods such as D-NeRF [S3, unofficial] and Nerfies [S4, unofficial] introduced explicit deformation fields to map between canonical and deformed spaces, improving controllability and handling non-rigid motion. The field has since expanded to include Gaussian Splatting variants [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial] and specialized applications like avatar reconstruction (DNRF [S4, unofficial], Skeleton-NeRF [S5, unofficial]).
